\h Matthew
\toc1 Matthew
\mt1 Matthew
\c 5
\s1 The Sermon on the Mount
\p
\v 1 One day as he saw the crowds gathering, Jesus went up on the mountainside and sat down. His disciples gathered around him,
\v 2 and he began to teach them.
\s1 The Beatitudes
\q1
\v 3 \wj “God blesses those who are poor and realize their need for him,\f + \ft Greek poor in spirit.\f*\wj*
\q2 \wj for the Kingdom of Heaven is theirs.\wj*
\q1
\v 4 \wj God blesses those who mourn,\wj*
\q2 \wj for they will be comforted.\wj*
\q1
\v 5 \wj God blesses those who are humble,\wj*
\q2 \wj for they will inherit the whole earth.\wj*
\q1
\v 6 \wj God blesses those who hunger and thirst for justice,\f + \ft Or for righteousness.\f*\wj*
\q2 \wj for they will be satisfied.\wj*
\q1
\v 7 \wj God blesses those who are merciful,\wj*
\q2 \wj for they will be shown mercy.\wj*
\q1
\v 8 \wj God blesses those whose hearts are pure,\wj*
\q2 \wj for they will see God.\wj*
\q1
\v 9 \wj God blesses those who work for peace,\wj*
\q2 \wj for they will be called the children of God.\wj*
\q1
\v 10 \wj God blesses those who are persecuted for doing right,\wj*
\q2 \wj for the Kingdom of Heaven is theirs.\wj*
\p
\v 11 \wj “God blesses you when people mock you and persecute you and lie about you and say all sorts of evil things against you because you are my followers.\wj*
\v 12 \wj Be happy about it! Be very glad! For a great reward awaits you in heaven. And remember, the ancient prophets were persecuted in the same way.\wj*
